WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.199 --> 00:00:03.480
Gary W. Goldstein: Whether I am a screenwriter
or some other form of creative, I think one

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:09.339
of the key disciplines is to understand that
discipline is key.

00:00:09.339 --> 00:00:13.710
And that is to say you should find out what
works best for you.

00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:16.020
Are you a morning person?

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:18.360
Are you a late night writer?

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:21.250
I’m not creative late at night.

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:27.800
I like being up but I’m not creative…I
write like a fiend when I have that early

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:33.890
morning coffee, because all night it has been
percolating for me (but that’s not true

00:00:33.890 --> 00:00:34.890
for everybody).

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:39.120
But if that is who you are, then make damn
certain that you’ve gone to bed at a reasonable

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:44.760
hour and that you’re up and you’ve gotten
your stuff done and now at 6:00 in the morning

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:48.500
or 7:00 in the morning or whatever it is,
you’ve set aside and you’ve turned your

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:55.500
phone off and that you’ve absolutely put
these soundproof walls around you (literally

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:02.149
and figuratively) so that you have two-three
hours of intensely productive time on a consistent

00:01:02.149 --> 00:01:03.149
daily basis.

00:01:03.149 --> 00:01:08.229
If you do that…because it’s a game of
inches…and if you do that, instead of being

00:01:08.229 --> 00:01:16.979
the person who is laboring over a script and
rewriting it for three years non-stop or you’re

00:01:16.979 --> 00:01:21.630
doing a lot of first drafts and you are on
your 12th script this year, those are not

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:23.469
the indicators of success.

00:01:23.469 --> 00:01:28.869
But if you’re someone who has got that kind
of discipline and you say ‘How much can

00:01:28.869 --> 00:01:30.270
I improve this?’

00:01:30.270 --> 00:01:33.820
We know that writing is rewriting, but up
to a point.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:35.899
So how many drafts?

00:01:35.899 --> 00:01:39.340
If I can do this every day and then I set
it aside and move onto the next one.

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:43.200
I may come back to that with proper inspiration.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:48.109
But if you can do that, what you can accomplish
in a short, one-year period will put to shame

00:01:48.109 --> 00:01:51.109
most people who don’t have that discipline.

00:01:51.109 --> 00:01:56.779
Who don’t know themselves and give themselves
a framework to be productive.

